<article class="env-lemma" id="01KN">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01KN">Lemma <span data-tag="01KN">26.21.15</span>.</a> An affine scheme is separated. A morphism from an affine scheme to another scheme is separated. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $U = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)$ be an affine scheme. Then $U \to \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(\mathbf{Z})$ has closed diagonal by Lemma <a href="/tag/01KI" data-tag="01KI">26.21.1</a>. Thus $U$ is separated by Definition <a href="/tag/01KK" data-tag="01KK">26.21.3</a>. If $U \to X$ is a morphism of schemes, then we can apply Lemma <a href="/tag/01KV" data-tag="01KV">26.21.13</a> to the morphisms $U \to X \to \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(\mathbf{Z})$ to conclude that $U \to X$ is separated. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>